posts.body:
Update: I think I figured out what was the problem.
Turns out, part of the problem was that I was editing the contents wrong. On the contents page, I was double clicking on the already existing command, believing that would open the highlighted one, when in reality it should've been right click + edit. Seems like I was adding a whole new command and just confusing the engine. I didn't know that you should be using right click + edit this whole time. :I
So the way I understand it, there should be a tick on "Skip if cannot move", and no tick on "Wait for completion" for This Event, and putting a tick on both for "Player", as per
@SGHarlekin
said. I think that was the sequence, but at the very least this got rid of the freezing.
@Solar_Flare
I honestly don't think my game will involve too much pushing obstacles as a gameplay feature, but I'll keep that in mind should I ever include a pushing puzzle or a game based around it, thanks.
@alasth
Turns out not putting a tick on "Direction fix" does indeed not conflict with the commands, it was what the tutorial told me to do so I just went along with it. I guess this saves a step though in the grand scheme of things.
Again-apologies for the really novice question-coding and syntax and programming was never my strong suit! Thanks for everyone's help!
